# Copy to .env and adjust. All values are optional; defaults are in scripts/lib.sh.

# Pinned Waze version to fetch/patch (default hardcoded in lib.sh). The patches only fit 5.23.0.2, so
# any other value stops the build unless WAZETRIPPER_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1 (for porting the hooks; set
# WAZE_VERSION_CODE to the matching versionCode too).
# WAZE_VERSION=5.23.0.2
# WAZE_VERSION_CODE=1030725
# WAZETRIPPER_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1

# Every build checks that apk/ is signed by Waze's own certificate and has the expected version.
# Optionally also pin the exact SHA-256 of apk/base.apk (the build prints it) to reject any other file.
# WAZE_BASE_SHA256=

# APK download source: apk-pure (default, no credentials) or google-play.
# APK_SOURCE=apk-pure

# Languages to bundle into the final apk: "all" (default) or a space-separated list, e.g. "pt en".
# LANGS=all

# fetch-apk and decompile skip their work when their outputs already exist. Set FORCE=1 (usually
# inline, e.g. `FORCE=1 scripts/all.sh`) to re-download and re-decompile from scratch.
# FORCE=1

# google-play only: an account email + AAS token (see apkeep USAGE-google-play.md).
# GOOGLE_EMAIL=someone@gmail.com
# AAS_TOKEN=xxxxxxxx
